What was taken: the idea of a bundled palette registry and the community palette
choices (Catppuccin, Dracula, Gruvbox, Solarized, Nord, Tokyo Night, Rosé Pine).
The palettes are the published colour values of those schemes, re-expressed as
about 20 colours each (src/artwork/palettes.ts) instead of ~380 hand-expanded tokens.

What was changed: no code is copied. The implementation is new and applies themes
through ctx.theme.overrideTokens (one reversible token layer) instead of writing
inline variables, has no !important rules, no polling and no host-class selectors.
The Codex/Claude brand themes, glass, composer, sidebar, session-title,
settings-skin and desktop-menu modules were not taken.

The Catppuccin, Dracula, Gruvbox, Solarized, Nord, Tokyo Night and Rosé Pine
palettes remain the property of their respective authors (all MIT-licensed).

UI controls (src/kit/) are adapted, via dsh-kit (https://github.com/deestax/dsh-kit), from
@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives (https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, packages/client/ui-primitives),
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek: markup, sizes and behaviour of Button, Switch, SegmentedControl, Input, Modal
and Tooltip, and the modal-layer and tooltip-placement helpers. The MIT permission notice is identical to the one in
this repository's LICENSE file and applies to those portions as well.

dsh-theme-endfield compatibility (src/shared/endfield.ts, src/client/endfield-dom.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Written against the public behaviour and variable names of dsh-theme-endfield
(https://github.com/ymh0000123/dsh-theme-endfield, MIT). No source is copied; the plugin is read at runtime
(its stylesheet selectors) and left unmodified.

Endfield look (src/shared/endfield-look.ts, src/client/endfield-look-css.ts, src/artwork/endfield-palettes.ts,
src/artwork/endfield-own-tokens.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A lighter port of the visible design of dsh-theme-endfield (https://github.com/ymh0000123/dsh-theme-endfield),
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 ymh0000123: square corners, the solid-accent controls, the hero wordmark, the
translucent composer and sidebar sheen, table and badge styling, and Endfield's paper/ink palettes. The rules
were rewritten (cheaper selectors, no runtime layout reads), and the token values used when colours are on Stock were
measured from a page running that plugin. The MIT permission notice is identical to the one in this repository's
LICENSE file and applies to those portions as well. "Arknights: Endfield" and its wordmark belong to their owners;
the wordmark text is drawn only while the Endfield look is switched on.

Glass (src/artwork/glass-tiers.ts, src/client/glass-css.ts, src/shared/glass.ts)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The glass setting (off / subtle / standard / strong) and its tier values come from dsh-theme-endfield
(https://github.com/ymh0000123/dsh-theme-endfield), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 ymh0000123: the fill opacities
(0.68 / 0.80 / 0.90 light, 0.64 / 0.76 / 0.88 dark), the backdrop blur radii (8 / 14 / 22 px), the white edge and sheen
alphas (0.65 / 0.35 light, 0.18 / 0.07 dark), the Endfield paper and ink fill colours, the surfaces it is applied to
(composer card without a backdrop filter, the open right panel with one, the sidebar's sheen and edge) and the
@supports and prefers-reduced-transparency fallbacks. The values were read from a page running that plugin; the
stylesheet is new (token-derived fills, one small sheet mounted only while glass is on). The MIT permission notice is
identical to the one in this repository's LICENSE file and applies to those portions as well.
